From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fil Dunsky <filipp.dunsky@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 01 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: allow the 743622 and 751472 errata on Cortina CS75xx

The CS75xx has a Cortex-A9 r2p1, which is affected by both errata. The
workarounds set bits in the CP15 diagnostic register, which is only
writable in the Secure state, so they are hidden on multiplatform
kernels. The CS75xx boot loader enters the kernel in the Secure state
(the kernel programs the Secure-only PL310 auxiliary control register),
and the vendor kernel set both bits on this SoC.

Signed-off-by: Fil Dunsky <filipp.dunsky@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/Kconfig
@@ -660,7 +660,7 @@ config ARM_ERRATA_720789
 config ARM_ERRATA_743622
 	bool "ARM errata: Faulty hazard checking in the Store Buffer may lead to data corruption"
 	depends on CPU_V7
-	depends on !ARCH_MULTIPLATFORM
+	depends on !ARCH_MULTIPLATFORM || ARCH_CORTINA_CS75XX
 	help
 	  This option enables the workaround for the 743622 Cortex-A9
 	  (r2p*) erratum. Under very rare conditions, a faulty
@@ -676,7 +676,7 @@ config ARM_ERRATA_743622
 config ARM_ERRATA_751472
 	bool "ARM errata: Interrupted ICIALLUIS may prevent completion of broadcasted operation"
 	depends on CPU_V7
-	depends on !ARCH_MULTIPLATFORM
+	depends on !ARCH_MULTIPLATFORM || ARCH_CORTINA_CS75XX
 	help
 	  This option enables the workaround for the 751472 Cortex-A9 (prior
 	  to r3p0) erratum. An interrupted ICIALLUIS operation may prevent the
